<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nimlot of Hermopolis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Namart</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nimlot, also read Namart, was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermopolis">Hermopolis</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a> in the later 8th century BCE, during the break-up of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s Third Intermediate Period. He joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tefnakht">Tefnakht</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> against the Kushite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a>, who besieged Hermopolis and forced his surrender. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victory-stela-of-piye">Victory Stela of Piye</a> describes the scene, including Piye's anger at the starving horses in Nimlot's stables.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nimlot-of-hermopolis.jpg" alt="Nimlot of Hermopolis" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste Mariette (1821-1881) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stele_Piye_submission_Mariette.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
